cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the R port and the original MATLAB SMIMfit library and paper."
title: "smimr: Stochastic Mobile-Immobile Model (SMIM) fits to solute breakthrough curves in R"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Liddick
    given-names: Mitchell J.
    email: mliddick@nd.edu
    affiliation: University of Notre Dame
version: 0.0.0.9000
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/freshwaterfather/smim-r"
abstract: >-
  An R port of the SMIMfit MATLAB library (Schmidt 2020; Volponi 2024) for fitting the
  truncated-power-law Stochastic Mobile-Immobile Model to conservative-tracer breakthrough
  curves, with scripted numerical-equivalence checks against the MATLAB original.
